See https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/issues/88543 for a repro and full context.

```cpp
void Float16ToFloat_ref(const float16* src, float* dst, size_t size) {
  for (size_t i = 0; i < size; i++) {
    dst[i] = cpu_half2float(src[i]);  // XXX: bug: assumes that src has enough elems to read from
  }
}
```

~~I think this needs to be fixed on the fbgemm side because these APIs are used in a bunch of places. And it's not possible to work around this in PyTorch without performing wasteful copies (wasteful because it can be mitigated with a check on the fbgemm side).~~
